rem Singleton Difference
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=136
rem Count the n below a limit for which
rem x^2 - y^2 - z^2 = n has exactly one
rem solution in arithmetic progression

use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 50000000

rem As in problem 135 with u v = n, one
rem solution occurs only for n = 4, 16,
rem a prime p = 3 mod 4, or 4 p and 16 p
rem for an odd prime p.
Ps = primes till Limit array
Odd = Ps greater 2
Mod3 = Ps mod 4 equal 3
Max = Limit - 1
By4 = Odd and Ps at most (Max // 4)
By16 = Odd and Ps at most (Max // 16)
Fix = array 4 16 at most Max
Answer = Mod3 count
Answer += By4 count
Answer += By16 count
Answer += Fix count
Answer print
